{
  "_about": [
    "Names the battle data used before it switched to Pokemon Showdown spellings on 2026-09-14.",
    "teammateNames: the OCR-era labels still found in the M6 days up to and including lastDate, and what each one means there. Applied to every Pokemon name of those days: the teammate column, the file's own 'pokemon' column and the snapshot key. Only valid inside that window: in those days \"Alolan Persian\" was the Kantonian Persian and \"Persian Form 1\" the Alolan one, while older seasons and the explorer metadata use \"Alolan Persian\" for the real Alolan forme. Likewise 11_09_2026 filed Floette-Eternal and Maushold-Four under the plain \"Floette\" and \"Maushold\" (the game has only those formes; the next day already says Floette-Eternal and Maushold-Four), while the plain names stay as they are in other seasons. Everywhere else a name is resolved against tools/showdown-species.json.",
    "catalogueNames: app catalogue (metadata) forms that are one ladder forme under another name, in every season: the app's only Floette is Floette-Eternal and its only Maushold is Maushold-Four (same stats, no other forme in the game). Their profile pages fold into the battle-data page of that name. Not Vivillon: the metadata's Icy Snow Pattern is a different pattern from the ladder's Vivillon-Fancy.",
    "retiredPageNames: extra old names whose /pokemon/<slug>/ pages were published and must keep redirecting (every teammateNames key is included automatically).",
    "retiredComparisonSlugs: old head-to-head URLs (/pokemon/<a>-vs-<b>/) that were published under the old names. The generator maps each side to its Showdown slug and writes a static redirect while that comparison page still exists.",
    "Read by tools/generate-manifest.mjs and tools/build_meta_trends.py."
  ],
